[[!meta title="Configuration of the production website"]]

Whenever you work on our website or documentation, you may need to
modify our ikiwiki configuration. You need to do so in 2 different
places:

 - The [[!tails_gitweb ikiwiki.setup]] configuration file that lives
   in our main Git repository is used for building:

    - the production website (built using GitLab CI)

    - the offline copy of the website that is included in every Tails release
      (built during the Tails build process)

 - Weblate's [staging website](https://staging.tails.net/) uses its
   own configuration file, which is managed by Puppet.

When you update [[!tails_gitweb ikiwiki.setup]], ask a Tails Team member to submit
your changes as a MR against the relevant files:

 - <https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/tpa/puppet-control/-/blob/production/site/profile/templates/tails/website/ikiwiki.setup.epp>.
 - <https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/tpa/puppet-control/-/blob/production/site/profile/files/tails/website/ikiwiki-libdir/IkiWiki/Plugin/sidebar2.pm>

Don't bother coordinating the merge of these 2 sets of changes. They can be
merged in any order without causing major trouble. What matters is that these
2 configurations stay in sync'.
